{"name":"Azores","hex":"#7c968b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Azores","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An archipelago of nine volcanic islands in the Atlantic Ocean.","An autonomous region of Portugal in the North Atlantic ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Azores"}],"entries":[{"title":"Azores","blocks":[{"text":"The Azores, officially the Autonomous Region of the Azores, is an archipelago of Portugal, in the Atlantic Ocean, about 1,400 km west of the Portuguese mainland. Politically and administratively, together with Madeira, it is one of the two autonomous regions of Portugal and a special territory of the European Union. It is the westernmost point and region of Portugal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Flag_of_the_Azores.svg/330px-Flag_of_the_Azores.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Azores"},{"title":"Azores (Assembly of the Republic constituency)","blocks":[{"text":"Azores is one of the 22 multi-member constituencies of the Assembly of the Republic, the national legislature of Portugal. The constituency was established in 1979 after Portugal's Atlantic islands were granted autonomy. It is conterminous with the autonomous region of Azores. The constituency currently elects five of the 230 members of the Assembly of the Republic using the closed party-list proportional representation electoral system. At the 2025 legislative election it had 230,289 registered electors."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Azores_in_its_region.svg/330px-Azores_in_its_region.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Azores_(Assembly_of_the_Republic_constituency)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Ribeira_Grande%2C_S%C3%A3o_Miguel_Island%2C_Azores_-_panoramio_%287%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Ribeira_Grande%2C_S%C3%A3o_Miguel_Island%2C_Azores_-_panoramio_%287%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Ribeira_Grande%2C_S%C3%A3o_Miguel_Island%2C_Azores_-_panoramio_%287%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Ribeira_Grande%2C_S%C3%A3o_Miguel_Island%2C_Azores_-_panoramio_%287%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gaspar Frutuoso wrote Saudades da Terra, the first history of the Azores and Macaronesia, in the 1580s.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARibeira_Grande%2C_S%C3%A3o_Miguel_Island%2C_Azores_-_panoramio_(7)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Henry_the_Navigator1.jpg/500px-Henry_the_Navigator1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Henry_the_Navigator1.jpg/500px-Henry_the_Navigator1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Under the direction of Prince Henry the Navigator, the Azores were discovered and populated in the early 1400s.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHenry_the_Navigator1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Desembarcoislasterceiras.jpg/500px-Desembarcoislasterceiras.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Desembarcoislasterceiras.jpg/500px-Desembarcoislasterceiras.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Battle of Terceira, part of the War of the Portuguese Succession","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADesembarcoislasterceiras.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/DpedroI-brasil-full.jpg/500px-Dped